    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/channels/employer/": {
      "title": "Employers",
      "description": "Employers – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Employers Westfield State is on the Handshake Recruiting Platform, a single website for campus recruiting. Post jobs and internships to over 1,500 schools reaching over 8M students Register for career fairs Manage your on-campus recruiting activities Login or create a Handshake account today! Coffee Chats Schedule a Dunkin’ coffee chat with a box of donuts to promote your organization in a high-traffic area. (Sept. 15 – Nov. 15, Feb. 15 – April 15) $50 (nonprofit), $100 (for profit) Employer Treks Host virtual or in-person company visits to inform students on a company’s mission, culture, and opportunities. $1500 for an in-person visit Snack Giveaway Snacks with a sticker of your logo and a QR code will be sent to a targeted student group (club, athletic team, etc.). $250 Coffee Sponsorship Provide coffee to students during final exams outside of the library. You’ll have the chance to boost student energy levels while interacting with students and promoting your organization. $500 Food Trucks Be a part of our Owl Appreciation Day in April by sponsoring a food truck . This is a great way to informally connect with students at a large, campus-wide event. $3500 Internships Interns work 8 to 40 hours per week, in paid or unpaid positions. Check out our Guide to Internship Programs (also see Virtual Internship Programs ). On-Campus & Mock Interviews Host mock interviews or interviews on-campus to connect with students in a more informal setting. Networking Nights Join us as a professional at one of our industry-specific networking nights.  You will connect with students seeking advice on entering the field. Social Media Take over our Instagram account for a day to share what a typical day is like and provide tips on careers in a variety of field.  Join our LinkedIn Careers Group to post opportunities directly to students and alums! Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/employer-sponsorship/": {
      "title": "Employer Sponsorship – Career Center",
      "description": "Employer Sponsorship – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Become a Sponsor Apply Today Build your employer brand by becoming a sponsor of the Westfield State University Career Center —WSU’s home for career planning and exploration, and the front-door to all career resources, data and information. By sponsoring the Career Center, you can showcase your brand to students, alumni and the campus community, 24x7x365, and demonstrate your commitment to supporting our collective investment into the career development for all students and recent grads. This partnership also creates a unique opportunity to engage with potential future employees early in their career journey, fostering long-term relationships and securing a competitive advantage in recruiting top talent. Check out the many benefits of sponsorship . ~5,000 Undergraduate & Graduate Students 23% Students of Color 41,000+ Alumni Association Members Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/register-for-a-career-fair/": {
      "title": "Register for a Career Fair",
      "description": "Register for a Career Fair – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Register for a Career Fair The Career Center assists employers in their efforts to connect with prospective employees through career fairs. We will host several career fairs throughout the academic year: Part-Time Job & Club Fair September 2026 4:00 pm – 6:00 pm Campus Green Counseling, Government & Criminal Justice Job Fair Wednesday, October 14, 2026 12:00 pm – 3:00 pm Scanlon Banquet Hall Business Job & Internship Fair Wednesday, October 14, 2026 12:00 pm – 3:00 pm Scanlon Banquet Hall – Loughman Living Room Job & Internship Fair February 2027 Scanlon Banquet Hall Healthcare Career Fair Spring 2027 Scanlon Banquet Hall Elevate departmental goals, one new hire at a time. register Today To register for a career fair, please log in or create an account with Handshake , click on “Fairs” then search for Westfield State University.  Once you complete the career fair registration, you will receive a confirmation email. Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/recruiting-options/": {
      "title": "Recruiting Options",
      "description": "Recruiting Options – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Recruiting Options Westfield State is on the Handshake Recruiting Platform, a single website for campus recruiting. Post jobs and internships to over 1,500 schools reaching over 8M students Register for career fairs Manage your on-campus recruiting activities Login or create a Handshake account today! Coffee Chats Schedule a Dunkin’ coffee and donuts chat to promote your organization (Sept. 15 – Nov. 15, Feb. 15 – April 15). $50 (nonprofit), $100 (for profit) Employer Treks Host virtual or in-person company visits to inform students on a company’s mission, culture, and opportunities. $1500 for an in-person visit Snack Giveaway Snacks with a sticker of your logo and a QR code will be sent to a targeted student group (club, athletic team, etc.). $250 Coffee Sponsorship Provide coffee to students during final exams outside of the library. You’ll have the chance to boost student energy levels while interacting with students and promoting your organization. $500 Food Trucks Be a part of our Owl Appreciation Day in April by sponsoring a food truck . This is a great way to informally connect with students at a large, campus-wide event. $3500 Internships Interns work 8 to 40 hours per week, in paid or unpaid positions. Check out our Guide to Internship Programs (also see Virtual Internship Programs ). On-Campus & Mock Interviews Host mock interviews or interviews on-campus to connect with students in a more informal setting. Networking Nights Join us as a professional at one of our industry-specific networking nights.  You will connect with students seeking advice on entering the field. Social Media Take over our Instagram account for a day to share what a typical day is like and provide tips on careers in a variety of field.  Join our LinkedIn Careers Group to post opportunities directly to students and alums! Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/channels/staff/": {
      "title": "Faculty & Staff",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Faculty & Staff Virtual Experiences Explore Job Market Hiring Trends News & Advice Virtual Experiences Networking Grab-and-Go Career Development Assignments Request a Presentation Disney College Program The Washington Center Faculty members and advisors often form strong relationships with students that are integral to a student’s personal, academic, and career success.  Students seek advice on issues ranging from majors, internships, graduate school, and professional direction. We look to partner with you on this process and have curated some resources to support you in your work: Integrate scalable project-based learning from world-leading companies into your curriculum for free. The Career Center has developed career development assignments and supplemental resources that you can easily embed into your syllabus. We can help you identify guest speakers for your class who can provide the employer/industry perspective. Simply reach out and we will do the rest! Access our virtual career center platform to view opportunities and career events. Explore Job Market Hiring Trends In partnership with Find a career that aligns with your career interests, see current salary projections, and identify skills you need to apply for that next job or internship. There are two ways to use this tool below: By Keyword: Search for the name of the occupation you’re interested in. By Industry: Not sure what job you’d like? Search by desired industry and see available occupations. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/channels/career-champion/": {
      "title": "Career Champions",
      "description": "Career Champions – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Career Champions Career Exploration Resumes & Cover Letters Virtual Case Studies with Top Employers Internship Search Job Search Explore Job Market Hiring Trends Featured Opportunities Interview Prep Graduate School LinkedIn & Networking Explore Career Paths & Current Job Market Explore Hiring Employers & In-Demand Jobs Virtual Case Studies with Top Employers On-Campus Employment What is a Career Champion? A Career Champion is a faculty or staff member who actively supports student career development by embedding career conversations, resources, and opportunities into their everyday interactions with students. Career Champions are not expected to serve as career counselors themselves, but rather to act as connectors, advocates, and encouragers who: Recognize the importance of career readiness as part of student success. Refer students to appropriate career services, tools, and experiential learning opportunities. Reinforce the development of skills, competencies, and professional habits in their teaching, advising, or mentoring. Role model lifelong learning, networking, and career exploration behaviors. Sidebar Become a Career Champion Request a Presentation Career Champion Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Career Paths by Major Employer Policies Featured Resources How-tos & Support Guides Interview Prep Resources Job Search Sites Networking Resources Online Tools Resume and Cover Letter Guides Westfield Handouts Close Clear Filters Regional Occupation Alignment Dashboard Share This: Share Regional Occupation Alignment Dashboard on Facebook Share Regional Occupation Alignment Dashboard on LinkedIn Share Regional Occupation Alignment Dashboard on X Copy Link The Regional Occupation Alignment Dashboard (ROAD) is designed to help state and regional leaders in workforce development, education, and policy … Read More Job Search Academy Share This: Share Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Job Search Academy on X Copy Link Westfield State University and Indeed are partnering to bring you the Job Search Academy , a program with all of Indeed’s … Read More Career Development Assignments Share This: Share Career Development Assignments on Facebook Share Career Development Assignments on LinkedIn Share Career Development Assignments on X Copy Link We’ve created career assignments covering a number of areas that can be used in your courses. We welcome you to … Read More The Washington Center Share This: Share The Washington Center on Facebook Share The Washington Center on LinkedIn Share The Washington Center on X Copy Link Learn more about Westfield State’s partnership with The Washington Center. Learn More Disney College Program Share This: Share Disney College Program on Facebook Share Disney College Program on LinkedIn Share Disney College Program on X Copy Link Learn more about Westfield State’s partnership with the Disney College Program. Learn More Career Outcomes Data Share This: Share Career Outcomes Data on Facebook Share Career Outcomes Data on LinkedIn Share Career Outcomes Data on X Copy Link Our Career Outcomes Data shows how Westfield State students turn their education into real-world success. Explore where our graduates are … View Outcomes Reports View All Resources Explore Job Market Hiring Trends In partnership with Find a career that aligns with your career interests, see current salary projections, and identify skills you need to apply for that next job or internship. There are two ways to use this tool below: By Keyword: Search for the name of the occupation you’re interested in. By Industry: Not sure what job you’d like? Search by desired industry and see available occupations. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
